                },
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                  "Text": "Stem metrics useful for plantation forestry are derive here from stem weight using an allometric relationship with stem diameter at breast height (DBH over bark). Basal area (BA, sum of areas of stems in m2 per ha) and stem height (Ht) depends on DBH, and volume (Vol over bark) is provide (g per ha) as a function of both Ht and BA. However, underbark metrics were also required, which necessitated the division of stem weight and volume into wood and bark components using, the volume component, which depends on bark thickness. All these functions are empirical and calibrated to provide adequate model skill. Finally, wood and bark densities are calculated. Tree stems are not exactly conical, and bark thickness and wood and bark densities vary radially and with height up the stem, with age, and between trees due to inter-tree competition and growth rate. All parameters, and even functions, can be redefined within genotype (cultivar) settings. \n     \r\n\r\n",
                  "Name": "Memo1",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Functions.LessThanFunction, Models",
                  "Name": "DBH",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Functions.VariableReference, Models",
                      "VariableName": "[Pinus].IndividualTreeStemWt",
                      "Name": "IndStemWt",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
                    },
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Functions.Constant, Models",
                      "FixedValue": 0.01,
                      "Units": null,
                      "Name": "MinimumIndStemWt",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
                    },
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Functions.Constant, Models",
                      "FixedValue": 2.0,
                      "Units": null,
                      "Name": "ElseMinimum",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
                    },
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Functions.ExpressionFunction, Models",
                      "Units": null,
                      "Expression": "[DBHEquation].Coefficient * ([Pinus].Stem.Vol/(([Pinus].Population+0.0001)*10000))^[DBHEquation].VolumeExponent * max(1.4, [Pinus].Stem.Ht)^[DBHEquation].HeightExponent * ((max(1.4, [Pinus].Stem.Ht)-1.3)/max(1.4, [Pinus].Stem.Ht))^[DBHEquation].TaperExponent",
                      "Name": "DBHEquation",
                      "ResourceName": null,
                      "Children": [
                        {
                          "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                          "Text": "DBH from per-tree stem volume v (m3) and height H (m), no Age: DBH = Coefficient x v^VolumeExponent x max(1.4, H)^HeightExponent x ((max(1.4, H) - 1.3)/max(1.4, H))^TaperExponent. Radiata 104.89 v^0.459 H^-0.31 ((H-1.3)/H)^0.292 fitted to 12,561 SwYG PSP measurements excluding OFO (quadratic mean DBH, residual SD 2.6%) (2026-11-16). The taper term makes DBH fall towards zero as trees approach breast height, as a cone-like stem requires; without it the equation over-predicted DBH of trees under 7 m tall by 7-14% in the PSP data and by 30-45% at Tarpeena and SETRES at age 4-7. OFO plots are excluded because their volumes are basal area x height / 3 scaled by a plot constant (a constant form factor of 0.32), not tree volumes; the earlier fit (103.39 v^0.459 H^-0.310) included them. Taeda 49.52 v^0.444 H^-0.057 and slash 74.26 v^0.436 H^-0.216 fitted to validation DBH; caribaea and hybrids 200 x sqrt(v/H) (constant form factor ~0.31; a steeper fitted form inflated FPQ DBH, pushed stands over MaximumSDI and cut volume); these set TaperExponent = 0.",
                          "Name": "Memo",
                          "ResourceName": null,
                          "Children": [],
                          "Enabled": true,
                          "ReadOnly": false
                        },
                        {
                          "$type": "Models.Functions.Constant, Models",
                          "FixedValue": 104.89,
                          "Units": null,
                          "Name": "Coefficient",
                          "ResourceName": null,
                          "Children": [],
                          "Enabled": true,
                          "ReadOnly": false
                        },
                        {
                          "$type": "Models.Functions.Constant, Models",
                          "FixedValue": 0.459,
                          "Units": null,
                          "Name": "VolumeExponent",
                          "ResourceName": null,
                          "Children": [],
                          "Enabled": true,
                          "ReadOnly": false
                        },
                        {
                          "$type": "Models.Functions.Constant, Models",
                          "FixedValue": -0.31,
                          "Units": null,
                          "Name": "HeightExponent",
                          "ResourceName": null,
                          "Children": [],
                          "Enabled": true,
                          "ReadOnly": false
                        },
                        {
                          "$type": "Models.Functions.Constant, Models",
                          "FixedValue": 0.292,
                          "Units": null,
                          "Name": "TaperExponent",
                          "ResourceName": null,
                          "Children": [],
                          "Enabled": true,
                          "ReadOnly": false
                        }
                      ],
                      "Enabled": true,
                      "ReadOnly": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "Enabled": true,
                  "ReadOnly": false
                },
                {
                  "$type": "Models.Functions.LessThanFunction, Models",
                  "Name": "BarkThickness",
                  "ResourceName": null,
                  "Children": [
                    {
                      "$type": "Models.Functions.VariableReference, Models",
